<b>Harbor</b>

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.380
Very impressive.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:56.320
You see, Kanamoney, once you're 
directing your third production,

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.030
you start to understand what the people want.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.830
And where are we with the story, Director?

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.160
Got it right here!

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:06.510
An enemy prisoner of war comes 
to understand human kindness,

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:12.170
changes sides, and fights 
alongside humanity!

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.750
<b>Soldier smiles,
but can't talk</b>

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.470
Can I stop you for a second?

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:29.140
What does the enemy look like?
 And who are they?

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:33.180
They're in UFOs, so they've 
gotta be aliens, right?

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.570
P-Probably?

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:37.330
The enemy fortress appears 
out of Lake Shibahama,

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:40.820
and has the same kind of design 
as the human towers. Why is that?

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.530
Actually, why were the UFOs attacking again?

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:46.810
Are they invading the Earth?

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.750
Figure it out!

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.930
Your directions dictate what 
the entire staff is doing!

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:56.330
You can fret your weird head off,
 but the clock is ticking!

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.970
If the storyboards take too long, that puts

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.090
extra pressure on every 
other step in the process!

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.220
Understand?!

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.930
I understand!

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:05.170
Asakusa melted her way into hiding!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:10.940
That sounds exciting!

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.360
Let's go to the Sound Club!

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:14.940
Open sesame!

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.200
<b>Fully Rotated</b>

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.200
<b>Fully Rotated</b>

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.200
<b>Fully Rotated</b>

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:36.590
<b>Rrrrrumble...</b>

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.660
It felt like we were lost in space.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:40.660
She's asleep.

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:42.330
A kappa?!

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:43.510
No. Human.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.090
You sounded like you were 
firing a beam in your sleep.

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:47.600
Like you'd see in a space battle.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.310
There's no sound in a vacuum, y'know.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.320
Wheel, dough.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:51.390
Well, duh.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.770
Wait, is it Saturday?!

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.580
Is today t-tomorrow?!

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:56.780
Today is tomorrow.

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:58.490
Oh, crap!

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:00.700
Tomorrow from yesterday, which was Thursday.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:03.370
It's still Friday.

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:07.280
Oh, man... so it's not tomorrow yet.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:10.980
Did you seriously think a whole day 
passed while you were asleep?

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.290
Well, I've never napped before.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.500
Wait, that was a lifetime first?!

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.490
Were you doing something on Saturday?

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:27.510
Good morning, comrades!

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:28.830
Morning!

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.610
You're sure you want to come along?

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.440
Why exactly are we meeting up on bikes?!

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.580
Because we're going sound hunting!

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.980
Let's hunt some sounds!

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.970
Work on the storyboards!

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:44.890
And figure out who the bad guys are!

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:48.240
Why are you tagging along on a sound hunt?!
 That's the audio director's job!

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.820
The general director's job is 
to keep an eye on everything!

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:54.240
Talk big after you finish 
your own damn job.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:57.150
I would've been fine on 
my own, but she insisted.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:58.580
I mean...

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.460
You clearly don't mean anything.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:01.500
But...

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:03.230
No ifs, ands, or buts.

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:04.080
Still...

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:05.690
No, not still! Moving!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.650
I-I'm just looking for 
ideas for the storyboards!

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.370
It's a hunt of my own.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.690
What hunt?

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:14.190
Scenario hunting!

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:17.530
I wanted one last idea to put a 
bow on the setup for the project.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.550
I don't mind the company, 
as long as you help out.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:22.250
Sounds good!

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:24.030
Why am I here?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.490
Let'sa go!

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:29.490
This had better be productive.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.910
<b>Turn on Lights</b>

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:07.710
This is the place.

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:09.590
Looks like the remains of a generator...

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:10.930
With English brick bonding.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.580
I can see the school!

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:19.620
I've been curious about 
this place for a long time.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:23.010
And this has something to do 
with the Shibahama-UFO Battle?

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:24.010
Probably!

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.570
No roof, huh?

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:30.940
The idea is the water comes down and 
turns a wheel, which generates power.

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:32.350
That's cool!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Six</b>

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Five</b>

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Seven</b>

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Four</b>

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Eight</b>

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Three</b>

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Nine</b>

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Two</b>

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Ten</b>

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>One</b>

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Eleven</b>

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:40.840
<b>Twelve</b>

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:38.110
Hey, it's the clock tower 
that we're always looking at!

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:40.840
Interesting to catch a glimpse up close.

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:43.110
This is one of the things I'm here for.

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:45.030
It's kinda like a tourist spot...

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:52.020
Oh, wow! It's a pendulum!

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:53.740
I wonder what this place was?

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:58.060
Looks to me an awful lot like an alien 
base disguised as a clock tower.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:01.250
It's so big! And you can 
see the back of the clock!

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.900
I'd wager the owners or some 
politician thought they'd

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.330
fix the place up and turn it 
into a tourist destination.

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:10.930
This building just gave me an idea!

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:16.100
<b>Twelve</b>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:19.430
<b>Three</b>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:19.430
<b>Eleven</b>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:19.430
<b>Ten</b>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:19.430
<b>Nine</b>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:19.430
<b>Eight</b>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:19.430
<b>Five</b>

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.770
It was once a luxurious home to wealthy tenants!

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:19.430
And inside the clock, high atop it,
 a massive treasure is hidden!

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:20.350
Thus...

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:29.590
An alliance of thieves has targeted it!

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.700
They face...

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.090
The bodyguard hired by the building's owners.

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:42.000
So a security guard, basically.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.750
The last scene is a duel atop the 
grass field that grows on the roof...

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.880
Stop. Hold it right there.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.090
This is one huge clock!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:53.530
How about that concept? It'd make 
for a great 15-minute short!

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:57.890
Stop talking about other projects. 
Focus on finishing the one you're working on.

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:01.200
What now?

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:03.140
<b>K</b>

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.140
There are Ks!

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.960
K? What?

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.970
You take the "K" from "kinetic 
energy" and call it a "K-cannon!"

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:22.660
<b>K</b>

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:11.740
It's a DEW the Imperial Army 
was cooking up in secret...

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.190
A <b>D</b>irected-<b>E</b>nergy <b>W</b>eapon!

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:15.930
Those are urban legends, right?

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:18.770
But then, it turns out, they're real!

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:22.680
And maybe this is the forgotten 
laboratory where it was worked on!

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.810
Gonna stop you right there again.

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:25.880
Get back on topic with our current project.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.580
I feel a guiding hand here...

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:31.860
This time, we're working something 
we were destined to make!

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:37.800
Essentially...

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:41.250
In our club room, on the 
other side of the coast,

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.850
the subject for an exposure 
test was being stored.

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:46.860
Something was fired from this side...

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:49.860
Which lit something in the eizouken club room

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:54.360
that kicked those fans we have 
into gear, to awaken something!

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.820
Asakusa's gone crazy!

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:59.660
<b>K</b>

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.660
I just figured out the 
connection to my storyboards!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:03.150
A mecha to fight those UFOs was
 developed right where we stand!

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:06.420
Basically, this was the base 
for the Shibahama military!

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.350
That sounds good to me.

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:12.320
See, Kanamori? This bit of sound 
hunting paid fine dividends!

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:13.840
Crap, my target!

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:16.200
Everybody, gimme a hand!

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:22.850
<b>K</b>

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:19.190
Kanamori, get the fluffy thing from my bag.

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:21.040
Asakusa, set up the tripod!

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:22.260
Roger Wilco!

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:26.340
Is this it?

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:28.410
Mizusaki, your jacket's kinda noisy.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:29.370
Really?

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:40.910
Almost time. Nobody move a muscle.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:15.030
Good work, everyone. That went smoothly.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:18.660
That was nerve-wracking!

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.430
I finally got it!

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.530
I'm surprised you didn't have it already.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:35.550
<b>K</b>

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.530
There's an old one in the club's collection,

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:28.670
but the sound has degraded with time.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:33.400
But even though everything else is 
in ruins, this bell still rings out.

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:35.550
It's probably just been forgotten about.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:38.550
It continues to ring for some reason?

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:43.560
That's magnificent!

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:45.620
All right,

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:49.350
the bell that continues to chime for 
some reason has given me a new idea!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:50.560
That's enough out of you!

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:07.610
I wanna go next!

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:09.550
Hey, eizouken.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.540
The class president!

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:14.670
Uh, no. I'm actually the secretary.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:19.760
So, did you figure out what to 
do about that stuff from before?

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:22.930
The copyrights of works belong 
to their individual creators.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:26.100
We'll enter Comet A as the film club,

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:30.020
and then any sales and collection of 
cash will be done on an individual basis.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.900
Couldn't you just enter a contest?

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.690
A contest would be good for our reputation,

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.400
but it'd take too long to pay dividends.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:41.220
An event like this gets us instant 
recognition, an influx of income,

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.630
and market research, all in one.

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:49.540
The eizouken's agenda is production 
and research, isn't it?

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.610
Management is a type of research, too.

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:54.470
The baseball club does that kind of thing.

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:59.840
They keep records of their sales, 
organize the data, and then report on it.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:01.710
It's only natural that popularity

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:06.150
would be the standard by which 
club activities are measured.

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:08.490
You could manage all that inside 
the school's jurisdiction.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:11.300
It wouldn't be anything more 
than a simulation, then.

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:14.620
Well, it's not exactly a model for society.

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:16.910
Schools are a world unto themselves.

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:19.940
Step too far outside of that world, 
and you won't be protected anymore.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:22.900
What're you getting at?

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:25.910
Behold!

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:30.830
We're moving beyond simple rotation!

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:32.970
Fans, drills...

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:36.690
propeller skirts, ducted fans, and chainsaws!

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:40.330
It's time we reconsider all 
of these spinning machines!

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:40.960
What is this thing?

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:42.630
Her job.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:43.770
This?

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:46.850
This motion is more like a gear.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.470
Like in a clock?

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.670
What is this? Wavy grass?

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:57.550
No, it's wavy sound.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:03.190
You layer it like this, the 
same way you would an image.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:06.200
I can hear it.

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:12.190
You knock it around, layer it, 
clip it up, and reattach it...

00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:14.610
What kind of tool is it supposed to be?

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:16.550
I'll think that up.

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:30.050
I've got it!

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:33.970
This equipment is said to be able 
to transmit wishes and gratitude

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:36.990
from the surface world to the underwater one!

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:39.650
<b>A device (ritual tool) that was created by using machine technology
 originally designed for milling</b>

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.230
<b>Top is a flat surface</b>

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.650
<b>Cylinder is made from bamboo,
 cut into quarters</b>

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:41.610
<b>Jet
Sometimes depicted as going up
 and down</b>

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:41.900
<b>Range of rotation is 
90 degrees, won't turn 
all the way at once</b>

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:43.400
And the water responds in kind by 
granting the surface world its blessing.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.440
<b>Wing</b>

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:42.480
<b>Axel catches water, 
causing the paddle to rotate</b>

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:42.610
<b>How the movement works</b>

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:42.690
<b>Axel</b>

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:42.690
<b>Stabilizer</b>

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:43.360
<b>Teeth will catch if there's
 ever reverse rotation. 
Lower axles also rotate.</b>

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:43.570
<b>Flow of water</b>

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.820
<b>Direction of piston movement</b>

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.740
<b>It's pushed in an undulating motion,
 so the axle moves upwards</b>

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:45.820
<b>The paddles move left and right, 
like a pendulum, when hit by
 the flow of water</b>

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:45.990
<b>Raised up by water's pull
 on the paddle, which is
 connected to the axe</b>

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.990
This device is what enables 
that mutual exchange!

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.990
<b>Output</b>

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:45.990
<b>Output</b>

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:45.990
<b>Input</b>

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:49.010
The tradition behind it is eventually forgotten,

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:51.410
but the technology itself evolves 
into becoming the basis for

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:52.950
clockwork machinery, and is passed on.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:54.720
And the bells?

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:56.230
Festival rites.

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:57.750
They purify people of their evil,

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.100
and call upon the water for a bountiful harvest.

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:11.850
The chime!

00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:00.730
I'm curious...

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:04.270
Does this have anything to 
do with our current project?

00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:06.520
Did you figure out how to connect this to it?

00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:08.620
You're really gonna need 
to decide on the villains,

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:10.710
or I won't be able to make 
much progress with the sounds.

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:14.120
What about the climax? Have you figured 
out the identity of the bad guys?

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:15.110
Not yet...

00:23:15.110 --> 00:23:19.000
And what are they after?! I thought you 
were gonna put a bow on the concept?!

00:23:23.970 --> 00:23:27.610
I forgot that they're in their own world, too.

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Illustration by:</b>
